# Draft CITATION.cff for the Bodley release. Not for the repository root until the owner approves (OWNER_DECISIONS.md).
# If .zenodo.json is also present, Zenodo's GitHub integration ignores this file for the archive record
# (help.zenodo.org/docs/github/describe-software/); GitHub still uses it for the "Cite this repository" box.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below. All statuses and claims in it are provisional, AI-produced and uncertified (human-certified count: 0)."
type: dataset
title: "Bodley: a provisional register of United States executive orders, their working statuses and source-hashed lifecycle claims (version 1)"
version: "1.0.0"
# OWNER: set to the publication date of the Zenodo version (YYYY-MM-DD). This is a draft date.
date-released: "2026-11-06"
authors:
  - family-names: Kind
    given-names: Danny
    affiliation: "NYU School of Law"
    # orcid: left blank on purpose; add "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000" when the owner supplies it
# OWNER: licence for the data. Recommendation CC-BY-4.0; alternative CC0-1.0 (decision D1).
# Code goes in LICENSE-CODE.txt (recommendation MIT; alternative Apache-2.0).
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/D3m0sthene5/Executive-Orders"
abstract: >-
  A register of 14,998 working bibliographic identities for United States executive orders (legal cutoff
  14 October 2026) with, for each, the source documents held, a provisional yes/no status for surviving
  operative effect, and for 1,527 orders a filed lifecycle claim with the source hashes and character spans
  it rests on. The number of orders certified by an independent human reviewer is 0; every status and claim
  is an AI-produced working hypothesis. No licensed text or bulk source bytes are included; sources are cited
  by URL and SHA-256.
keywords:
  - executive orders
  - presidential power
  - legal history
  - United States
  - executive order revocation
  - executive order longevity
  - provenance
  - provisional data
references:
  - type: data
    authors:
      - family-names: Thrower
        given-names: Sharece
    title: "Replication Data for: To Revoke or Not Revoke? The Political Determinants of Executive Order Longevity"
    year: 2016
